## System Prompt Engineering

The system prompt had a significant effect on Phi-4-mini performance. Key findings:

| Change | Local score | Delta |
|---|---|---|
| Baseline (code prompt, no SymPy rule) | 36/63 | — |
| + SymPy float conversion rule | 38/63 | +2 |
| + GF(p) Galois field guidance + trig rules (over-extended) | 33/63 | –5 |
| Reverted to SymPy rule only | 38/63 | +5 |
| "verify" prompt | 22/63 | –16 |

**Lesson:** Phi-4-mini (3.8B) is sensitive to system prompt length. Adding more than ~2–3 lines of additional guidance caused regressions on other questions. The final effective prompt is the shortest version that includes only the critical SymPy float conversion rule.

