## What Worked vs. What Didn't

### What worked
- **Domain-specific dense retrieval** over a curated MathWorld corpus, far outperforming live web search
- **Phi-4-mini at full precision** over larger models at 4-bit — inference speed within the time limit matters
- **Code executor with SymPy** for algebraic/calculus/probability computation
- **Short, focused system prompts** — every added line risks regression on a 3.8B model
- **SymPy float conversion rule** — single most impactful prompt change (+2 local questions)

### What didn't work
- **Math-specialised models** (Qwen-Math, Mathstral) — general instruction following is more important than math fine-tuning for a mixed competition
- **Large models with 4-bit quantization** — speed/precision tradeoff goes against large quantized models
- **Extended system prompts** — adding GF(p) and trig guidance caused –5 regression
- **BM25 retrieval fixes** — both the dense-veto and dense-gate fixes were too aggressive, tripling zero-score online games
- **Hybrid retrieval** — BM25 introduces false positives (keyword collisions like "salt"→Salinon, "assembly"→Assembly Number) that outweigh the gains
- **Option verification prompt** — reframing generation as constraint verification is harder than forward computation for a 3.8B model; catastrophic –16 local regression
